  "note": "Cbt Gp option 2: one strong BG covers the entire front by occupying DLs on the likely approaches, its basic aim to inflict cas and delay; the second BG kept concentrated for manoeuvre and the destruction of the En; the third used to prevent the En enveloping or outflanking the DL (p 17 para 28 a (2)). Concept and Conduct of SZ Battle (C&SC handout, SZB): a Cbt Gp is an all-arms group on an Armd or Mech Bde HQ, armour heavy with at least two Armr Regts or mech heavy with at least two MIBs (p 5 para 9 g); for the C Tps an Armd Bde with 1-2 HAT Bns, or a Mech Bde with a HAT Bn and an Armr Regt (p 12 para 23 a). The SZ is divided into sectors, a BG to each (p 4 para 9 a); a Cbt Gp on 60-70 km (p 13 para 24 a). The options assume air, arty and AD support (p 16 para 28). The DLs 9 km apart, the BHOL 6 km behind the last DL, a BG's posn 3 km deep: a decision (E: the handout draws no scale).",
